    "ffi_driver_async_collectors_ignore_transferred_and_consumed_readable_tokens",
    "ffi_driver_async_collection_cancels_pending_reads_after_its_observer_is_discarded",
    "ffi_driver_collection_waits_for_all_active_borrows_and_explicit_disposal_rejects_safely",
    "ffi_driver_borrow_ownership_returns_with_the_result_before_background_task_exit",
    "ffi_driver_retirement_releases_waiting_collectors_and_borrow_guards_once"
  ],
  "behavior": {
    "construction": "Host::new_for_driver installs owner-stack Dispatcher and composes one memory-free private resource disposal helper against original nominal type aliases. Resolve actual instantiated ResourceType and Func pairs after instantiation. Legacy constructors retain prior composition/limits. No invented async factory types for ordinary resource worlds.",
    "disposal": "DriverClient::drop_resource takes complete owned wire descriptor. C resource-drop uses value. Guest/host kind remains distinct even for identical token text. Host references validate type/token/generation and embedding ownership before commit. Destructor trap retires Store; preflight failures preserve owners.",
    "collection": "DriverClient::collect_resource and C resource-collect accept typed guest/host collector requests; ignore stale/transferred/old generation capabilities. Accepted disposal/collection survives observer drop; callbacks retain operation origin and fresh poll token.",
    "borrowGuards": "Driver export argument lowering records borrowed resource keys. Scoped guards hold counts until result publication; reject concurrent owned transfer or explicit disposal of a borrowed owner. GC collection waits with native registered wakers and revalidates ownership after all borrowers return. Retirement releases guards and waiting collectors once.",
    "resultBoundary": "Maintained Wasmtime task_complete validates resource scope and commits lender decrements before sending its result. Actual early-return guest test releases borrow ownership while a post-return import remains suspended. Native guard registry stores token strings/counts/wakers only; no JS values or snapshots.",
    "readableCollection": "DriverClient::collect_async_value and C collect ignore consumed/closed/transferred future/stream descriptors. Pending reads use existing close cancellation/ownership protocol; discarded cleanup observer still executes. Explicit close keeps validation errors.",
    "limits": "Private resource helper has no linear memory and adds one core instance only when resources exist. Shared Store fuel/instance limits apply; legacy constructors do not add the helper."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "TypeScript traced per-origin frames, ALS/first-JS-error routing, owned future/stream wrappers, producer interfaces and runtime deferred cleanup integration remain unfinished.",
    "Legacy C resource-drop/collect and HTTP entries still reject persistent handles. New resource commands do not migrate HTTP or switch the TypeScript runtime.",
    "No new combined compiler/static-runtime/native engine/guest adapter/moving-GC qualification or platform/package validation is claimed. ABI/runtime sources match the previous C-driver checkpoint; its runtime regressions remain separate evidence.",
    "Async import borrowed-resource forwarding remains to be investigated and exercised before runtime migration: current take_borrows removes callback tokens from the registry before awaiting callback completion.",
    "Turnloop provider sources remain immutable validation patches; no releases performed.",
    "Shipping-lock crypto-bigint RUSTSEC-2026-0387 remains open; manifests/shipping lock unchanged; no audit waiver or publish-age override.",
    "Full goal remains active; no readiness, release or merge authorization inferred."
  ],
  "developmentFailuresRetained": [
    "v261 test needed explicit u64 parse type because serde_json adds PartialEq implementations",
    "v268 Accessor Access exposes data_mut, not data; fixed guard acquisition without changing semantics",
    "negative borrow harness initially expected a later retired-state assertion; the test instead caught borrower reply id2 where only rejected disposal id4 should arrive; terminal expected101 result audited without rerun"
  ],
